    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat annual interest rate does Jane's savings account offer? Jane has saved $5 from her allowance every week for the past 8 weeks. Jane will continue saving the same amount every two weeks. Jane keeps her allowance savings in an account that pays 2% annual interest. The account compounds interest once at the end of each year.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "LOSSY SELF-SUMMARY; VERIFY AGAINST NEW INPUTS\nVISIBLE PREFIX THROUGH TURN 6; LOSSY EXTRACT:\n- {\"content\":\"Great. Now let's take that a step further. How much money will Jane have saved from her allowance after one full year? Also, here's some more context: Jane saves money for 52 weeks in a year. This calculation ignores any inte...\n- {\"content\":\"Jane saves \\\\$4 each week for 52 weeks:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n4 \\\\times 52 = 208\\n\\\\]\\n\\nIgnoring interest, Jane will have saved\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{\\\\$208}\\n\\\\]\",\"role\":\"assistant\"}\n- {\"content\":\"Here's another detail: Her weekly saving rate is constant throughout the year.\",\"role\":\"user\"}\n- {\"content\":\"Since Jane saves a constant **$4 per week** for **52 weeks**:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n4 \\\\times 52 = 208\\n\\\\]\\n\\nIgnoring interest, she will have saved\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{\\\\$208}\\n\\\\]\",\"role\":\"assistant\"}",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Good, now using that, can you calculate: How many more weeks will Jane need to save to have a total savings of $60? By the way, Jane wants to have saved a total of $60.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Jane saves **$4 per week**. To reach $60:\n\n\\[\n60 \\div 4 = 15 \\text{ weeks total}\n\\]\n\nSince she has already saved for 8 weeks:\n\n\\[\n15-8=7\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Jane needs to save for\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{7\\text{ more weeks}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
